---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navigation from '../components/Navigation.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
const interests = [
  { title: 'Poker', text: 'I like reading GTO charts to understand the reasoning underneath the ranges. That also helps me think about when to depart from them, because the person across the table is not playing perfectly either.', href: '/personal#poker', link: 'The variants we play' },
  { title: 'Writing', text: 'Mostly I write to find out what I think. Sometimes a sentence comes out clearer than the thought that started it. I keep poems and prose here, along with lines from books I want to remember.', href: '/personal#writing', link: 'Poems and prose' },
  { title: 'Basketball', text: 'I like to think there is a little Kyrie in my step, though I would not push the comparison. My favourite part is the wordless coordination: a look across the court or a small gesture that changes the play.' },
  { title: 'Games', text: 'Before grinding for wins, I want to understand why the system works the way it does. Usually that turns out to help. Then I can make a plan and change it when it stops working.' },
];
---
<Layout title="About — Mingxi Yan" description="I started coding after starting university. A little about how I learn, what I build, and what I do outside work.">
  <Navigation />
  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="page-shell about-opening">
      <p class="eyebrow">A little about me</p>
      <h1>I came to code late.</h1>
      <div class="about-story">
        <p>I wrote my first line of code after starting university. Everyone around me seemed to have been programming since they were twelve. For a while, that felt like a gap I would never close.</p>
        <p>But learning it late means I still remember where it was confusing. That helps when I teach, and when I build something that someone else has to understand. The work I am happiest with is the kind I could explain to the version of me who did not get it yet.</p>
        <p>I am now a fifth-year master’s student at Carnegie Mellon’s Language Technologies Institute. I work on AI systems, from the data and tools around a model to how we evaluate its behavior.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/work">Experience, research, and projects ↗</a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="page-shell about-interests">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Outside the work</p><h2>What else I spend time on</h2></div></div>
      <div class="about-grid">{interests.map(item => <article><h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.text}</p>{item.href && <a class="text-link" href={item.href}>{item.link} ↗</a>}</article>)}</div>
    </section>
    <section class="page-shell about-closing">
      <p class="eyebrow">What I’m looking for</p><h2>Careful engineering.<br />A problem worth solving.</h2>
      <p>I like working where AI systems meet actual people. The question is what it takes for the whole system to work, including the parts around the model.</p>
      <p>I am also happy to talk about technology, game theory, philosophy, or a poker hand you cannot stop thinking about.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="mailto:mingxiy66@gmail.com">Send me a note ↗</a>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
